SUMMARY:Biomedical Informatics for Computer Scientists
LOCATION:White 411\, Case Western Reserve University
DESCRIPTION:A one-hour introduction to biomedical informatics for computer 
 science students. The lecture connects familiar computing problems to clin
 ical workflows and introduces the standards\, software\, shared infrastruc
 ture\, and communities already available in healthcare. The goal is to hel
 p future developers recognize when they can build on existing work—and k
 now where to look—rather than reinventing data models\, interfaces\, or 
 isolated proprietary solutions. Students will leave with starting points f
 or further learning\, projects\, and research. No medical background is re
 quired.
